    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on darwin1859-ch13-16: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.61";
    dc:description "Morphological similarity through ontogeny has a clear quantitative test. Existing public data cover selected vertebrates and insects, not the stated breadth.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Use stage-matched embryo images or landmark data to compare within-class interspecific morphological distances during development with adult distances and test association with ecological conditions. Lower embryonic than adult disparity and weak embryo-environment association support the claim.";
